Manage the distributions of a Nexo server (Admin API, admin:ManageDistributions):
a bucket, or a prefix of it, exposed on custom domains as a website (index
document, SPA fallback, error pages, redirects, behaviors per path, signed URLs)
or as an S3 endpoint. The changes reach every node of a cluster without restart.

Every change reads the distribution, changes it and writes it back guarded by
its ETag: a concurrent change is retried. Point the DNS of the domains (CNAME,
A/AAAA) to the cluster or to the proxies in front of it.

Usage:
  nexoctl dist [flags]
  nexoctl dist [command]

Available Commands:
  behavior      Manage the behaviors per path of a distribution
  cache         Manage the cache settings of a distribution, its domains and paths
  cert          Manage the TLS certificates of the domains of the distributions
  create        Create a distribution
  disable       Disable a distribution (its domains answer 403)
  domain        Add and remove the domains (aliases) of a distribution
  edit          Change the origin, the mode or the default behavior of a distribution
  enable        Enable a distribution
  error-page    Replace the error answers of a distribution with pages
  export        Export distributions as YAML
  headers       Set the response headers and the CORS policy of a distribution
  import        Create or replace the distributions of a YAML file
  info          Show a distribution
  invalidate    Invalidate cached content of a distribution
  keygroup      Manage the key groups of the signed URLs and cookies
  list          List the distributions
  origin-secret Manage the origin secret of the proxies in front of the cluster
  redirect      Manage the redirections of a distribution
  remove        Remove a distribution
  resolve       Show what serves a host (distribution, virtual host, S3 API)
  restrict      Restrict the clients of a distribution (source IP, origin secret, rate limit)
  sign-url      Sign a URL (or cookies) of a signed behavior
  test          Show how a distribution serves a URL: behavior, access, headers

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for dist

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl dist [command] --help" for more information about a command.
